## Why This Is Asked
Production anomaly systems face non-stationarity, sparse labels, and strict latency. This question tests end-to-end design, from data schema to deployment, plus practical techniques like self-supervised pretraining and online adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Self-supervised pretraining for unlabeled streams
- Online adaptation with meta-learning
- Two-tower architecture for heterogeneous features
- Drift detection and safe rollout/rollback
- Latency budgeting and quantization

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example gating logic for latency-adaptive routing
function route(payload, limitMs) {
  const t0 = performance.now();
  const score = computeScore(payload);
  const dt = performance.now() - t0;
  if (dt > limitMs) return 'fallback';
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate drift detectors in an AB test?
- What failure modes could cause late anomaly alerts and how to mitigate?

## Why This Question Is Asked
Evaluates the ability to design real-world, latency-constrained explainability systems that balance privacy and governance requirements in high-stakes ML environments.

## Key Concepts
- Per-instance explanations under strict latency constraints
- Privacy-preserving attribution without raw feature exposure
- Caching, bucketing, and surrogate models for performance optimization
- Drift monitoring and governance compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
function attribution(event) {
  const bucket = features.map(f => bucketize(f.value, f.schema));
  const fingerprint = hash(bucket);
  const cached = cache.get(fingerprint);
  if (cached) return cached;
  const attribution = surrogate.predict(bucket);
  cache.set(fingerprint, attribution);
  return attribution;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical multi-task learning under streaming constraints, including feature hashing, online updates, drift detection, calibration, and retraining cadence.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-task learning with shared representations
- Online learning with partial_fit
- Feature hashing for high-cardinality categoricals
- Drift detection (PSI, drift in AUC)
- Latency and memory constraints, calibration

